🚽 Test case: #193 -- returning a struct POINTER where a by-value struct
🚽 return is expected (`bussin pp;` with `gang Point *pp`) is a type error,
🚽 not an implicit dereference (PR #253 review, finding 1).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};

gang Point deref(gang Point *pp) {
    bussin pp;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Point q;
    q.x = 5;
    gang Point r = deref(&q);
    bussin 0;
}
